/*
 * Unused for now. The idea is that a duck would land, chill out, lower stress, then leave. They would leave if a dangerous event
 *  starts, giving the player a heads up. They can leave by being pulled under the water by something, giving stress. I'd probably
 *  remove this since it's so similar to the ducklings event. I'm learning that variation isn't always good, since variation can imply
 *  different mechanics to the player, when in reality there is none.
 */
:: Fishing Duck Arrive
<<if $bus is "fishingMoor">>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.duck.phase to "present">>
	<<set $daily.fishing.moor.duck.age to 0>>
	<<fishingLocationDescription "moor">>
<<else>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.lake.duck.phase to "present">>
	<<set $daily.fishing.lake.duck.age to 0>>
	<<fishingLocationDescription "forestLake">>
<</if>>
<br><br>

A loose group of ducks sweeps low over the water and splashes down ahead of you, sending rings spreading out across the surface.
<br><br>

<<if $bus is "fishingMoor">>
	<<link [[Wait for a bite (0:05)|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Wait for a bite (0:05)|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><<run stopFishingProp()>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Widgets Fishing Duck Wait Ambient [widget]
<<widget "fishingDuckWaitAmbient">>
	<<if _args[0] is "moor">>
		<<set $daily.fishing.moor.duck.age to $daily.fishing.moor.duck.age + 1>>
		<<set _duckAge to $daily.fishing.moor.duck.age>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.lake.duck.age to $daily.fishing.lake.duck.age + 1>>
		<<set _duckAge to $daily.fishing.lake.duck.age>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _duckLeaveChance to Math.min(0.5, _duckAge * 0.04)>>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent 10>>
		The duck drifts slowly across the water, quacking occasionally.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The duck flaps its wings vigorously, sending up a small spray.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The duck bobs gently on the ripples, riding the small waves.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The duck upends itself into the water, feet skyward, before surfacing with a brisk shake.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The duck shakes its head, scattering water drops.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent _duckLeaveChance>>
		One of the ducks flaps hard against the water and lifts off. A second follows, then a third, until the whole group is airborne, climbing away in a loose, rattling line until they're out of sight.
		<<if _args[0] is "moor">>
			<<set $daily.fishing.moor.duck.phase to "finished">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $daily.fishing.lake.duck.phase to "finished">>
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent 0.05>>
		There's a sudden violent churn of water. One duck vanishes, nothing left but a burst of loose feathers spinning above the surface. The others erupt into the air in a clatter of wings, calling sharply as they scatter and disappear.
		<<if _args[0] is "moor">>
			<<set $daily.fishing.moor.duck.phase to "finished">>
		<<else>>
			<<set $daily.fishing.lake.duck.phase to "finished">>
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
<</widget>>
